// Transitive param-type propagation.
//
// THE BUG. ir_collect_param_types learns a parameter's type from call sites, but reseeded `st`
// from DECLARED types on every round -- so what it learned about one function was never available
// when it walked that function's body. An inferred type therefore stopped after one hop:
//
//     main -> cfwd(CPt, CPt)     learned
//     cfwd -> cdot(p, q)         p/q still unknown here, so cdot resolved to NOTHING
//
// The consequence was silent data corruption, not slow code. Field OFFSETS still resolve (a slot
// comes from the global name->slot map and needs no struct type), so the GEPs were right and only
// the field TYPE was lost. The multiply then went through nova_rt_mul, which integer-multiplies
// two double bit patterns: bits(1.5) and bits(3.0) each carry 51 trailing zero bits, so the
// product had more than 64 and the answer was EXACTLY 0. Nothing crashed.
//
// Asserted by value AND structurally. The value catches the 0; the structure catches the case
// where the answer is right but every float op went through dynamic dispatch, which no value
// assertion can see and which is the entire point of 3.1.

type CPt
    cx: float
    cy: float

// Reached ONLY through cfwd -- there is no direct call to it anywhere in this program.
fn cdot(a, b)
    a.cx * b.cx + a.cy * b.cy

fn cfwd(p, q)
    cdot(p, q)

// Two hops, so this proves a real fixpoint rather than one extra hardcoded level.
fn cfwd2(p, q)
    cfwd(p, q)

// ── THE SOUNDNESS DIRECTION ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Chaining must not propagate a type past the point where it stops being true. `cur` starts as
// `root` (a dict) and is REASSIGNED on every hop, so after the first one it is whatever the
// previous hop returned -- here a nested dict, then a LIST. `pget` is genuinely polymorphic and
// must stay generic.
//
// This is the shape that broke std/core/getin: the warm-up inference ran a single pass, which
// visits blocks in order, so it harvested `pget(cur, ...)` as "dict" from the seed and never saw
// the reassignment contradict it. `cur[k]` then specialized to nova_rt_dict_get, which returns 0
// for a LIST hop -- get_in(d, ["a","b",1]) gave 0 instead of 20. Silent wrong data.
fn pget(c, k)
    c[k]

fn walk(root, path)
    let cur = root
    let n = len(path)
    for i in 0..n
        cur = pget(cur, path[i])
    cur

fn main()
    let p = CPt { cx: 1.5, cy: 2.5 }
    let q = CPt { cx: 3.0, cy: 4.0 }

    // 1.5*3.0 + 2.5*4.0 = 4.5 + 10.0 = 14.5
    print("chain1 " + str(cfwd(p, q)))
    print("chain2 " + str(cfwd2(p, q)))

    // dict -> dict -> list index. 20 iff pget stayed generic.
    let d = {"a": {"b": [10, 20]}}
    print("widen " + str(walk(d, ["a", "b", 1])))
